# RaSP index-build leftovers. Excluded 2026-09-30, after they broke CD on the deploy host.
#
# `data/*.sqlite` does NOT match a `.sqlite.building` name, and there was no `*.zip` rule, so the two
# largest files on the VM -- the 10.05 GB `df_rasp_gnomad_clinvar.sqlite.building` the builder writes
# before swapping it in, and the 9.04 GB proteome source zip -- entered the build context during an
# on-server index rebuild and `COPY data ./data` shipped them into a layer. Observed: run 36710716430
# died with "no space left on device" writing /app/data/df_rasp_gnomad_clinvar.sqlite.building, run
# 36719593581 the same writing /app/data/rasp_preds_alphafold_..._v2.zip, and run 36697775556 was
# OOM-killed (rc=137) mid-build -- on a disk the 62 GB of accumulated build cache had already filled.
#
# The exclusion costs nothing: ../data is bind-mounted at /app/data at runtime, so a copied copy is
# shadowed anyway. It is insurance rather than a speedup -- it only bites during a rebuild, which is
# exactly when the failure happened. Keep the small JSONs below unignored, or `COPY data ./data` has
# nothing to copy and the seed layer breaks.
data/*.building
data/*.zip

dist
logs
.cache
__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Tooling, agent and local-analysis leftovers. These are gitignored, but they SURVIVE a
# `git checkout --force` on the deploy path, and the build context there is the PARENT directory — so
# without these the daemon is sent hundreds of megabytes of unrelated files. Measured on the audit
# machine: scratch/ 352.8 MB, .zvec-grep/ 116.4 MB, .antigravity/ 81.7 MB, graphify-out/ 64.5 MB,
# .kilo/ 49.0 MB, coverage/ 16.7 MB.
scratch
.zvec-grep
.antigravity
graphify-out
.kilo
.gemini
graft
coverage
temp_jobs
